  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency response to vulnerable people in under-served areas</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtltspangt*Througlt/spangtltspangth the Emergency Response Project for Vulnerable People, the needs of vulnerable people, including those with disabilities and those who have lost the ability to work due to a new health condition, will be responded to. Therefore, we will focus on people whose lives and livelihoods have become directly at risk as a result of prolonged displacement, poor economic conditions, hyperinflation, escalating hostilities.) During the project&#x2019;s life span of 10 months.lt/spangtlt/pgtltpgtEach mobile team includes a dedicated team specialized in dealing with people in need and trained in protection basics, in addition to survey staff and specialized team in distributing GIKAMIKA items.ltbrgtThe project visits the following areas within two mobile teams:ltbrgt1- Eastern Kweiresltbrgt2- Al-Zurbaltbrgt3- As-Safiraltbrgt4- Al-Hadher.ltbrgtThe project will work to encourage the local community to participate in implementing its activities.ltbrgtIts services include providing food assistance: Providing food assistance to people in need and. The project will provide home delivery services for the food basketltbrgtNutrition: A comprehensive nutritional survey to identify cases of malnutrition and acute malnutrition and refer them to (Entities that provide therapeutic services for malnutrition cases (nutritional supplements, medications, etc.)ltbrgtAs for protection, the protection sector services (gender-based violence) are summarized in: Providing gender-based violence response services and making them available to victims of gender-based violence and women and girls at risk in addition to psychosocial support sessions and legal advice in addition for community initiatives in addition for distributing General and medical In-Kind Assistance. ( GIKA MIKA )lt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
